# Dance Maniax (G*874 VER. JAA), Konami 2000: test mode's I/O CHECK, from what dmx-install left (its NVRAM). Attract by
# ~8000; Test at 8500 opens the MAIN MENU on I/O CHECK; Start at 9200. Then each input in turn,
# held 40 frames, with a snapshot while it is held: player 1's sensors (D-SENSOR U L/R, D0 L, D1 L,
# D0 R, D1 R), Select L/R, player 2's the same, then 2P Start; each shows ON in its own place.
# 1P and 2P Start together leave it (to the MAIN MENU). Hashes the main RAM every frame, to compare
# HIRAKU's 573 core with MAME, and checks the input map against the game's own test.
game dmx

hash ram  0x80000000 0x80400000   # 4 MiB main RAM (KSEG0)

at 8500 press "Service Mode" 8
at 9200 press "1 Player Start" 8
at 9400 press "P1 D-Sensor U L" 40
at 9420 snap
at 9460 press "P1 D-Sensor U R" 40
at 9480 snap
at 9520 press "P1 D-Sensor D0 L" 40
at 9540 snap
at 9580 press "P1 D-Sensor D1 L" 40
at 9600 snap
at 9640 press "P1 D-Sensor D0 R" 40
at 9660 snap
at 9700 press "P1 D-Sensor D1 R" 40
at 9720 snap
at 9760 press "P1 Select L" 40
at 9780 snap
at 9820 press "P1 Select R" 40
at 9840 snap
at 9880 press "P2 D-Sensor U L" 40
at 9900 snap
at 9940 press "P2 D-Sensor U R" 40
at 9960 snap
at 10000 press "P2 D-Sensor D0 L" 40
at 10020 snap
at 10060 press "P2 D-Sensor D1 L" 40
at 10080 snap
at 10120 press "P2 D-Sensor D0 R" 40
at 10140 snap
at 10180 press "P2 D-Sensor D1 R" 40
at 10200 snap
at 10240 press "P2 Select L" 40
at 10260 snap
at 10300 press "P2 Select R" 40
at 10320 snap
at 10360 press "2 Players Start" 40
at 10380 snap
at 10420 press "1 Player Start" 20
at 10420 press "2 Players Start" 20
at 10540 snap
at 10600 quit
